<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/undated">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siege of Urshu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/urshu">Urshu</a> was a siege by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittites</a> of the city of Urshu in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, recorded in a Hittite text. The siege documents Hittite use of tunnelling techniques. The Hittites, however, generally preferred political isolation of enemies to costly direct assaults.</p></div>
